<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qungrat</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kungrad, Qongrat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qungrat are a Turkic tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, descended from the Mongol Qongirat of the 13th century. Within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> and the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> confederation they were powerful in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>: the Sufid dynasty of the 14th century sprang from them, and the Qungrat dynasty ruled the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> from 1804 until 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qungrat.jpg" alt="Qungrat" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khiruge · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khongirads_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
